rustype (0.2.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix a GNOME Shell crash when typing in VTE terminals on GNOME 45 to 48.
  * Do not delete text that the application has already removed.
  * Keep the letters after a deliberate double tone key (tesst gives test).
  * Exit with status 1 from --doctor when a check fails.
  * Settings: refresh lists at once and read the config as the engine does.
  * Installer: finish cleanup after service errors.
  * Windows: compose capitals with Shift and Caps Lock.

 -- Nam Tran <support@namtr.dev>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 20:41:48 +0700

rustype (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add a Ctrl+Shift toggle for Vietnamese.
  * Accept tone keys f, j and x typed before the vowel.
  * Add Simple Telex, Quick Telex and automatic sentence capitalisation.
  * Add always-off applications through app_modes.
  * Restart the service automatically after a failure.
  * Settings: saving no longer removes options it does not manage.
  * Windows: process keys injected by other software.

 -- Nam Tran <support@namtr.dev>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 10:35:11 +0700

rustype (0.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Replace the IBus engine with rustype-linux, one process for GNOME.
  * Usable right after installation, without logging out.
  * Fix typing in the Chrome address bar.
  * Fix VNI spelling of ươ after h, kh and th (hương, thường, thước).
  * Accept Vietnamese syllables that were treated as English words
    (môn, nôn, bể, bổ, mổ, rôm, sên, têm).
  * Start normally when a stale address file names an unrelated process.
  * Settings: deleted macros and words no longer come back.

 -- Nam Tran <support@namtr.dev>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 00:20:12 +0700

rustype (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release of Rustype for Debian and Ubuntu.
  * Ultra-lightweight pure Rust input method server for GNOME (~2.5 MB RAM).
  * Comprehensive Telex and VNI input methods with 14,710 golden test cases.
  * Native GTK4 + Libadwaita settings application (rustype-settings).
  * Built-in system diagnostics tool (rustype-linux --doctor).
  * GNOME HIG squircle icon set across standard FreeDesktop resolutions.
  * GNOME Shell focus tracking extension.

 -- Nam Tran <support@namtr.dev>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 15:30:00 +0700
